WEBVTT

00:09.801 --> 00:13.221
DECEMBER 2020

00:14.305 --> 00:16.975
JINNAM BOXING

01:26.669 --> 01:28.505
Oh, uh, sir.

01:28.588 --> 01:31.299
You need to wear a mask on the bus, sir.

01:31.382 --> 01:33.676
You can't ride the bus
without a mask. I'm sorry.

01:33.760 --> 01:34.636
Let's go.

01:34.719 --> 01:36.679
You'll be allowed on
when you return with a mask.

01:36.763 --> 01:38.515
Who are you to tell me what to do?

01:38.598 --> 01:40.975
- We get penalized--
- What? A mask?

01:42.227 --> 01:44.270
- It's my choice!
- Please leave, sir.

01:44.854 --> 01:47.232
You're a driver,
so drive the damn bus.

01:47.315 --> 01:48.316
I'm telling you.

01:48.399 --> 01:51.569
- Please put on a mask and come back, sir.
- You're just a driver. Come here!

01:52.112 --> 01:54.322
- There are passengers on board.
- Please don't do this.

01:54.405 --> 01:56.616
- What the hell is this? Whoa!
- Whoa!

01:56.699 --> 01:58.827
- Sorry. Sorry.
- Get off of me.

01:59.619 --> 02:01.079
What? Who the hell are you?

02:01.162 --> 02:03.665
I'm sorry, I think
you'll have to walk home. Sorry.

02:03.748 --> 02:05.250
I'm sorry.

02:05.333 --> 02:07.377
You shi--

02:07.460 --> 02:09.254
Sorry, sir.

02:09.337 --> 02:11.256
I'm very sorry.

02:11.339 --> 02:12.632
Whoa, I'm sorry.

02:12.715 --> 02:14.509
I hope you're not hurt. Sorry, sir.

02:17.804 --> 02:19.305
Goddamn you little--

02:19.889 --> 02:20.890
I'm very sorry.

02:22.142 --> 02:23.268
Bullshit.

02:24.811 --> 02:26.980
- I'm really sorry.
- My ass.

02:31.234 --> 02:33.069
Sorry about that. Thank you.

02:33.153 --> 02:34.904
- Thank you, sir.
- No problem.

02:36.990 --> 02:40.118
See,
the passengers are grateful too.

02:59.345 --> 03:01.264
The guy in the mask kept saying…

03:21.993 --> 03:23.703
I'm so sorry.

03:24.204 --> 03:27.749
God, I had no idea it would go on
for this long.

03:28.958 --> 03:31.211
I am so sorry that I have to ask you.

03:31.294 --> 03:32.128
I'm sorry.

03:32.212 --> 03:34.797
I'll try to put something together
next month. I promise.

03:35.882 --> 03:39.969
So, do you think can you wait
just one more month?

03:41.137 --> 03:43.014
I… I promise I'll pay you back.

03:43.848 --> 03:46.768
Yes, yes. Next month. I'll try my best.

03:47.352 --> 03:48.686
Yes, thank you.

04:27.058 --> 04:30.937
BLOODHOUNDS

04:33.940 --> 04:35.942
Amidst the ongoing recession
brought on by COVID-19…

04:36.025 --> 04:38.027
CITIZENS TREMBLE WITH ANXIETY
ABOUT ABANDONED BUILDINGS IN THE CITY

04:38.111 --> 04:41.114
…a suspended building construction project
is threatening the safety of the citizens.

04:41.197 --> 04:42.156
NO TRESPASSING

04:42.198 --> 04:44.701
Construction on the building
you see behind me had been suspended twice

04:44.784 --> 04:47.412
due to on-site workers being diagnosed
with COVID-19.

04:47.495 --> 04:49.622
When the company went bankrupt,
the building was abandoned

04:49.706 --> 04:51.624
becoming an eyesore
in the middle of the city.

04:51.708 --> 04:54.377
Seoul City must act quickly
to resolve this situation.

05:02.093 --> 05:05.221
In the United States, over 3.5 million
hotel employees were laid off

05:05.305 --> 05:06.723
in the third quarter alone.

05:06.806 --> 05:08.850
I'm telling you
that for the next three to for years

05:08.933 --> 05:12.145
there will be no foreign companies
interested in acquiring this hotel.

05:12.645 --> 05:13.896
Domestic companies even less so.

05:13.980 --> 05:15.898
You make these claims
as though they're facts.

05:15.982 --> 05:17.859
I have a lot of friends
who are future leaders

05:17.942 --> 05:19.694
of Korea's top fifty corporations.

05:19.777 --> 05:22.405
I have thoroughly discussed it with them
and reached this conclusion,

05:22.488 --> 05:24.490
so these claims are highly likely
to be factual.

05:25.366 --> 05:26.200
Actually,

05:27.243 --> 05:28.578
they are simply facts.

05:29.287 --> 05:31.998
You'd be doing well to negotiate with me,
Mr. Vice President.

05:32.081 --> 05:32.957
Mr. Hong.

05:34.083 --> 05:37.670
As you know, our bank has already lent
400 billion won to this building.

05:37.754 --> 05:40.173
Stating you will only be paying back
300 isn't a negotiation.

05:40.256 --> 05:43.217
Shouldn't one be prepared to accept
some losses in the current situation?

05:43.801 --> 05:45.094
How else can business be done?

05:45.720 --> 05:48.723
I am not a businessman,
but I am the banker.

05:49.349 --> 05:51.851
Uh, Mr. Director, Mr. Vice President,

05:51.934 --> 05:53.853
the reason I brought the two of you
over here…

05:53.936 --> 05:54.771
Yes.

05:54.854 --> 05:58.066
…is to push for a speedy completion
of the construction work on the building

05:58.149 --> 05:59.442
for the citizens' safety.

05:59.525 --> 06:01.402
Talking to him
is like talking to a brick wall.

06:01.486 --> 06:04.072
If you're suggesting
that I'm being unreasonable,

06:04.155 --> 06:06.741
let me ask you this,
which part of what you said is reasonable?

06:15.666 --> 06:17.752
I must apologize for my tardiness.

06:18.586 --> 06:21.756
This is Mr. Kim Myeong-gil.
I mentioned him before our meal.

06:22.256 --> 06:23.299
May I introduce you.

06:23.383 --> 06:26.386
Assemblyman Seo Woo-hyeon,
a close acquaintance of the mayor,

06:26.969 --> 06:28.638
introduced him to us.

06:29.472 --> 06:30.640
Kim Myeong-gil.

06:32.809 --> 06:34.894
KIM MYEONG-GIL

06:35.895 --> 06:37.855
I'll contact you individually later today.

06:38.481 --> 06:39.315
Okay.

06:44.028 --> 06:44.904
Kim Myeong-gil.

06:55.790 --> 06:58.167
Excuse me,
but what kind of work do you do?

06:59.168 --> 07:00.920
Primarily I deal with investments.

07:01.003 --> 07:03.214
When good people request my assistance,

07:03.297 --> 07:05.591
I help them out
to the best of my abilities.

07:05.675 --> 07:08.094
So are you a moneylender?

07:09.137 --> 07:12.265
Hey, did you know
that this man's a loan shark?

07:13.141 --> 07:15.518
Mr. Kim dabbles in various lines of work.

07:15.601 --> 07:18.062
You really think this is the right place
to bring this predator?

07:20.440 --> 07:23.151
And you must be the eldest son
of Chairman Hong Woo-geun.

07:24.485 --> 07:27.488
When I was young, I worked for someone
named Chairman Bang in Myeong-dong.

07:28.281 --> 07:30.616
You wouldn't remember
since you were a baby at that time,

07:30.700 --> 07:32.827
but when the IMF crisis hit Korea,

07:32.910 --> 07:35.913
Iil Group nearly went bankrupt
because they didn't have six billion

07:35.997 --> 07:37.498
after fifty years in business.

07:38.040 --> 07:41.878
Back then, Chairman Hong Woo-geun
went to my boss, Chairman Bang,

07:41.961 --> 07:43.504
to ask for assistance.

07:43.588 --> 07:46.048
He got down on his knees
saying he had to save the company

07:46.132 --> 07:47.133
at whatever cost.

07:47.675 --> 07:50.720
And with all his sincerity
and his passion,

07:50.803 --> 07:51.804
he got to Chairman Bang.

07:53.139 --> 07:53.973
So then,

07:54.557 --> 07:56.642
I filled up a bag
with six billion in cash,

07:56.726 --> 07:57.894
and I went over to your house.

07:58.686 --> 08:02.523
I also remember your mother prepared
some refreshing Korean melon for me

08:02.607 --> 08:03.774
to express her gratitude.

08:05.109 --> 08:08.112
There is no dirty money
unless it's used for nefarious agendas,

08:08.196 --> 08:10.781
but when used for good,
that makes it good money.

08:11.365 --> 08:14.243
I came here
to extend what support I have to offer.

08:17.997 --> 08:20.500
How are the negotiations?

08:21.167 --> 08:23.920
There were differences
in the amount they had in mind.

08:24.003 --> 08:27.256
- So we were just talking.
- Ah… How much of discrepancy?

08:27.340 --> 08:28.508
A hundred billion.

08:32.720 --> 08:36.641
Mr. Hong, do you plan on overseeing
hotel operations yourself?

08:36.724 --> 08:39.477
I got my master's in hotel management
in Switzerland

08:39.977 --> 08:41.479
and worked for four years in Hong Kong.

08:41.562 --> 08:43.689
I see you are well-prepared.

08:45.274 --> 08:48.486
With your permission,
I would like to make an investment.

08:48.569 --> 08:51.280
What's your offer?

08:51.364 --> 08:55.826
Well… you need 100 billion,
so I'll invest that much.

08:59.372 --> 09:02.166
If need be, I will invest more.

09:02.250 --> 09:03.209
What are the terms?

09:03.292 --> 09:04.126
Right.

09:04.669 --> 09:05.962
There are only three.

09:06.504 --> 09:09.465
First off,
I would like to have a small casino

09:09.966 --> 09:12.218
built on the highest floor
of the hotel's structure.

09:12.301 --> 09:14.845
Just as you dream of managing a hotel,
Mr. Hong,

09:14.929 --> 09:17.473
well, I dream of operating my own casino.

09:18.474 --> 09:19.600
And secondly,

09:19.684 --> 09:23.604
I ask that you help me set up a small bar
in the basement of the hotel.

09:23.688 --> 09:25.273
The last thing is,

09:25.356 --> 09:27.400
if something like COVID-19
were to spread again,

09:27.483 --> 09:30.861
I would like our hotel
to be a quarantine space.

09:30.945 --> 09:33.656
for those without money,
and it will be free of charge.

09:34.532 --> 09:35.783
The harder the times get,

09:35.866 --> 09:38.536
the more we all should be looking out
for one another.

09:38.619 --> 09:41.789
Because… that's how we build
a better world.

09:46.085 --> 09:47.753
The 100 billion won investment

09:48.546 --> 09:50.756
can be available to you
as early as tomorrow.

10:06.731 --> 10:08.608
It went well?

10:10.026 --> 10:11.861
- Mm-hm.
- So they'll bite?

10:12.445 --> 10:15.781
Mm.

10:16.365 --> 10:17.199
Oh yay!

10:17.283 --> 10:20.328
So I guess I need to start thinking
about how I want to decorate the bar!

10:20.411 --> 10:22.955
Well, uh, people don't go to bars
to see how they're decorated.

10:23.039 --> 10:24.582
They go to see the girls.

10:24.665 --> 10:26.500
So you better get busy
hiring some pretty girls.

10:27.084 --> 10:29.170
No, I think you should get busy,
you fucker.

10:29.253 --> 10:32.256
You know, it would be better
if you could talk as nice as you look.

10:32.340 --> 10:34.175
What would you know? You prick!

10:37.678 --> 10:39.055
I need to wipe my face.

10:39.639 --> 10:40.473
Oh.

10:43.434 --> 10:44.268
Here you go.

10:59.784 --> 11:00.826
Let's get going.

11:05.247 --> 11:06.749
How's the Seongeun Building?

11:06.832 --> 11:10.044
None of the tenants have any ties
to the police or prosecutor's office.

11:10.127 --> 11:11.420
Did you also check in-laws?

11:11.504 --> 11:14.173
Yes, of course. I told you
I only overlooked it that one time.

11:14.256 --> 11:16.342
Someone could have a partner who's a cop.

11:16.842 --> 11:18.594
Do your job well
so he doesn't have to worry.

11:18.678 --> 11:20.554
Ah, why don't you worry about yourself?

11:21.055 --> 11:22.139
Jang-do,

11:23.307 --> 11:25.643
you should speak to my woman
with more respect.

11:26.936 --> 11:28.646
Yes, you're right. I'm sorry, sir.

11:28.729 --> 11:30.648
Hey, apologize to me, you asshole.

11:31.691 --> 11:33.776
This asshole apologizes to you, ma'am.

11:33.859 --> 11:36.529
Hurry up, please.
I could really use a drink.

11:36.612 --> 11:37.571
Yes, sir.

11:39.907 --> 11:42.868
This is the 2020 KBFC
Rookie of the Year Tournament.

11:42.952 --> 11:44.829
The Rookie of the Year Tournament
is supposed to be held

11:44.912 --> 11:48.332
amidst the loud shouting and cheering
of fans expressing their love and support,

11:48.416 --> 11:50.543
but due to COVID-19,
there are no spectators today.

11:50.626 --> 11:52.461
It feels rather gloomy in here,
don't you think?

11:52.545 --> 11:53.379
That's right.

11:53.462 --> 11:55.589
The Rookie of the Year tournament
is normally a rowdy affair

11:55.673 --> 11:56.882
with lots of cheering for everyone.

11:58.259 --> 12:01.345
As we speak, we begin
the third round of Hong Woo-jin's match.

12:01.429 --> 12:03.013
Now we have a middleweight match here

12:03.097 --> 12:04.640
with Hong Woo-jin in the red trunks,

12:04.724 --> 12:06.726
going up against Jung Jae-hun
in the blue trunks.

12:06.809 --> 12:07.643
Get in there.

12:07.727 --> 12:09.603
Great combination of body shots.

12:09.687 --> 12:11.939
Now we see Hong Woo-jin
leaning against the ropes.

12:12.022 --> 12:14.024
He provokes his opponent
after landing body shots.

12:14.108 --> 12:16.318
Would you look at that provocation.

12:16.402 --> 12:18.487
I mean, I wouldn't go near.

12:18.571 --> 12:20.281
Whoa, a body shot!

12:20.364 --> 12:22.491
A clean hit to the body.

12:22.575 --> 12:24.326
He landed a blow to the face.

12:24.410 --> 12:26.579
He knocks his opponent down! Hong Woo-jin!

12:26.662 --> 12:29.081
Whoa! A double right
followed by a one-two strike.

12:29.165 --> 12:32.001
Look at that footwork.
He has great showmanship.

12:32.084 --> 12:33.335
Whoa, it's a KO.

12:33.878 --> 12:34.837
KIM RAE-HYEON
KIM GUN-WOO

12:34.920 --> 12:37.506
We have Kim Gun-woo
going up against Kim Rae-hyeon.

12:37.590 --> 12:40.092
Kim Gun-woo in blue, everybody,
the super rookie in blue trunks.

12:40.176 --> 12:43.554
Kim Gun-woo is looking
for a chance with his guard up.

12:43.637 --> 12:45.598
- A body blow!
- He goes to his knees!

12:45.681 --> 12:48.184
That's right.
A precision blow to the solar plexus…

12:48.267 --> 12:50.227
- That's the end of the match.
- Indeed.

12:50.311 --> 12:52.104
Ending with just one blow.

12:52.188 --> 12:54.982
Kim Gun-woo mows down his opponent
with a single blow again.

12:55.065 --> 12:56.525
He's a matchless competitor.

12:56.609 --> 12:58.110
A terrifying rookie has emerged.

12:58.194 --> 13:00.488
Things are already getting heated.

13:00.571 --> 13:02.323
He's getting cornered.

13:05.284 --> 13:08.287
He grabs him and throws him over.
He threw his opponent down.

13:08.370 --> 13:09.914
That was against the rules.

13:09.997 --> 13:13.417
- He did it first.
- He's too agitated now.

13:13.501 --> 13:15.503
- Box!
- Let's do this!

13:15.586 --> 13:18.339
He parts his hair.
Hong's showmanship is unmatched.

13:18.422 --> 13:20.299
That is Hong Woo-jin for you.

13:20.382 --> 13:21.926
He provokes. He dodges.

13:22.009 --> 13:23.302
Wow! Look at him dodge!

13:25.763 --> 13:28.724
Here he goes again…
He connects! We have a knockdown!

13:28.808 --> 13:30.559
It's Hong Woo-jin's specialty.

13:30.643 --> 13:32.186
A double jab followed by a straight!

13:32.269 --> 13:34.021
Hong Woo-jin, the marine.

13:34.104 --> 13:35.314
Hong Woo-jin advances again.

13:35.397 --> 13:36.440
HONG WOO-JIN

13:36.524 --> 13:37.483
Go lower.

13:37.566 --> 13:39.902
A match between
Kim Gun-woo and Lee Yong-gyu.

13:41.654 --> 13:44.406
Kim Gun-woo in the red trunks
is built like a tank.

13:44.490 --> 13:45.825
He dodges both blows.

13:45.908 --> 13:48.494
Kim Gun-woo's strength lies in infighting.

13:48.577 --> 13:51.413
He is leveraging his skills
in close-range hitting.

13:51.497 --> 13:53.582
Another punch, and he dodges.

13:53.666 --> 13:57.503
A body shot! He brings down his opponent
with one blow!

13:57.586 --> 13:59.129
A left hook to the body.

13:59.213 --> 14:01.423
I had that level of talent
when I was a contender.

14:01.507 --> 14:03.592
- Are you all right?
- Yeah.

14:03.676 --> 14:06.095
That's why you won a gold medal.

14:06.846 --> 14:08.556
Now, Kim Gun-woo versus Hong Woo-jin.

14:08.639 --> 14:11.308
- Yeah, let's see.
- Let's find out who takes home the trophy.

14:11.392 --> 14:14.061
No big moves.
Short punches. Use your waist!

14:14.144 --> 14:16.897
Watch out for his left hook.
His punches are no joke.

14:23.779 --> 14:26.282
Bro, I'm a marine.

14:26.365 --> 14:27.199
THE STRONGEST

14:27.283 --> 14:28.534
Watch out for his left hook.

14:28.617 --> 14:30.953
And I'm telling you,
I'm an invincible marine.

14:31.036 --> 14:34.123
Okay, but don't cry
if you get the shit beat out of you.

14:34.206 --> 14:35.040
All right?

14:39.086 --> 14:40.880
- Let's go!
- You got this.

14:40.963 --> 14:41.797
Keep your hands up.

14:41.881 --> 14:43.591
Come forward to meet.

14:43.674 --> 14:45.843
Now good luck to you both.
To your corners.

14:50.014 --> 14:52.516
His fighting up until now
has truly been a marvel.

14:52.600 --> 14:55.728
Kim Gun-woo, the super rookie,
has a very unique fighting style.

14:55.811 --> 14:57.938
That's right.
Kim Gun-woo is an infighter

14:58.022 --> 14:59.481
that's good against other infighters.

14:59.565 --> 15:01.025
Right.

15:01.108 --> 15:02.234
On the other hand,

15:02.318 --> 15:05.696
Hong Woo-jin is an out-boxer
with a counter up his sleeve.

15:05.779 --> 15:07.990
That's right.
Hong Woo-jin knows how to have fun

15:08.073 --> 15:09.158
during his matches.

15:09.241 --> 15:10.451
On the other hand,

15:10.534 --> 15:13.078
we have his opponent
who stoically plays it by the book.

15:13.162 --> 15:15.873
He's going in! He's going!
He's cornering him!

15:15.956 --> 15:18.542
Can Hong Woo-jin get out?
Can he get out of this?

15:18.626 --> 15:20.711
Wow! He got out of that really well.

15:20.794 --> 15:23.589
Hong Woo-jin is just remarkably fast.

15:23.672 --> 15:26.467
And since Kim Gun-woo
is also a middleweight…

15:26.550 --> 15:28.677
Wow,
he goes for a wild swing!

15:28.761 --> 15:31.096
Here we go. He guards the body shot.

15:31.180 --> 15:33.057
Kim Gun-woo has a great defense.

15:33.140 --> 15:35.392
- Doesn't he?
- He's like a rock.

15:35.476 --> 15:36.977
And he keeps on guarding.

15:37.061 --> 15:38.729
Uppercut!

15:38.812 --> 15:40.522
He landed that one.

15:40.606 --> 15:41.815
Indeed he did.

15:41.899 --> 15:43.525
What a performance this is.

15:43.609 --> 15:45.986
A right hook! Wow, what a dodge.

15:46.987 --> 15:50.115
Hong Woo-jin is
constantly applying nonstop pressure.

15:50.950 --> 15:53.369
- Another left.
- Can he recover?

15:53.452 --> 15:55.412
And Hong Woo-jin-- He goes down.

15:55.496 --> 15:57.665
- He's down!
- One… two…

15:57.748 --> 15:59.667
- Three… four
- With stomach blows,

15:59.750 --> 16:01.126
the shock does not come right away.

16:01.210 --> 16:04.254
It takes around five seconds.
That is when it hits.

16:04.338 --> 16:06.298
Six, seven…

16:06.382 --> 16:08.133
He gets up
after five seconds.

16:08.217 --> 16:09.843
He recovered well from that one.

16:09.927 --> 16:10.844
Yes, he did.

16:10.928 --> 16:12.972
But that has definitely got to sting.

16:13.055 --> 16:15.349
There's going to be an aftereffect.

16:15.432 --> 16:16.475
I think so.

16:17.267 --> 16:18.102
Come on.

16:20.187 --> 16:23.607
Come on!

16:48.215 --> 16:49.049
Come on.

16:49.758 --> 16:52.094
Hey… come get some.

16:53.762 --> 16:54.930
Son of a bitch.

16:57.933 --> 16:59.935
Come get me!

17:01.645 --> 17:03.147
Will he take the bait?

17:03.230 --> 17:05.399
- Kim Gun-woo has a lot to think about.
- Come on!

17:05.482 --> 17:07.776
And there he goes! Will he connect?

17:07.860 --> 17:11.196
Stop! One, two…

17:11.280 --> 17:13.615
Three… four…

17:13.699 --> 17:15.451
His tactics really backfired.

17:15.534 --> 17:16.368
KO!

17:16.452 --> 17:18.120
Kim Gun-woo went in for the kill

17:18.203 --> 17:21.832
and ended the match
once again with the same body shot.

17:21.915 --> 17:24.334
I'll tell you something.
That body shot is ruthless.

17:28.505 --> 17:29.631
You all right?

17:30.466 --> 17:32.885
I have tainted the honor
of my fellow marines.

17:33.469 --> 17:35.137
A blow to the liver will do that.

17:36.472 --> 17:37.681
Okay, I'm out of here.

17:38.515 --> 17:39.933
What about dinner, huh?

17:40.642 --> 17:41.852
There's the pandemic.

17:42.436 --> 17:44.146
I mean,
your boy has just gone through a lot.

17:44.229 --> 17:45.606
The least you can do is feed him.

18:01.497 --> 18:02.956
Go home and order in.

18:06.168 --> 18:07.002
Later.

18:19.139 --> 18:20.015
Oh.

18:23.268 --> 18:24.895
What? Huh? What?

18:25.896 --> 18:26.897
Wanna grab a bite?

18:27.648 --> 18:29.316
Why would I wanna grab food with you?

18:29.900 --> 18:32.319
I was gonna get some pork belly.
Thought you might want some.

18:35.656 --> 18:36.615
Are you pitying me?

18:37.199 --> 18:38.033
No.

18:38.117 --> 18:40.244
Go ask those other assholes you KO'd
to eat with you.

18:40.327 --> 18:41.954
But they all went home.

18:56.718 --> 18:58.846
- Wasn't the prize money ten million?
- Yeah.

19:00.305 --> 19:02.099
Then why settle for pork belly?

19:02.182 --> 19:03.433
Let's get rib eye.

19:03.517 --> 19:06.186
- I'm only going to spend 50,000.
- Why?

19:06.270 --> 19:08.021
I need to give the rest to my mom.

19:08.105 --> 19:10.149
- Do you owe your mom money?
- No.

19:10.232 --> 19:11.108
Then why?

19:11.608 --> 19:13.485
I have to pay the rent for her store.

19:14.361 --> 19:15.445
You're a good son.

19:16.238 --> 19:17.656
Just spend an extra 10,000.

19:17.739 --> 19:20.325
This barbecue buffet I know
charges 29,000 a person.

19:20.409 --> 19:22.077
It's insane, and they serve Korean beef.

19:22.161 --> 19:23.996
- You serious?
- Of course not, idiot.

19:25.581 --> 19:28.542
How could they afford
to serve Korean beef that cheap?

19:28.625 --> 19:30.419
Do you spend all your time working out?

19:31.503 --> 19:33.922
Anyway, that buffet is all right.
Just spend a little more.

19:34.006 --> 19:34.840
No.

19:37.301 --> 19:38.135
Hey.

19:48.103 --> 19:48.937
Let's go.

19:50.522 --> 19:52.149
How is your left hook so strong?

19:53.025 --> 19:54.651
Back when I worked part-time
at a junkyard,

19:54.735 --> 19:56.069
I practiced my hooks on a tire.

19:56.153 --> 19:57.321
Just your left?

19:58.447 --> 19:59.823
Why would I only work on my left?

19:59.907 --> 20:01.909
No, I'm asking
if you only worked on your left.

20:01.992 --> 20:03.827
No, of course I hit with both hands.

20:03.911 --> 20:05.579
Then why is your left so strong?

20:05.662 --> 20:08.916
- Actually, my right is stronger.
- Then why use only your left?

20:08.999 --> 20:11.335
Because I couldn't find a good time
to use my right.

20:12.669 --> 20:13.587
What a show-off.

20:14.630 --> 20:15.464
You think so?

20:15.547 --> 20:17.716
You're saying you could take
everyone down with just your left.

20:18.300 --> 20:19.509
At least today, yes.

20:19.593 --> 20:21.428
Yeah, see? What a show-off.

20:22.012 --> 20:23.388
Actually, I consider myself humble.

20:23.472 --> 20:24.348
Flip the pork already.

20:24.431 --> 20:26.350
Not yet. It needs 30 more seconds.

20:26.433 --> 20:28.185
Well, I think it's ready now.

20:28.268 --> 20:30.270
You're wrong.
I worked part-time at a barbecue place.

20:30.354 --> 20:31.396
I know my meat.

20:31.480 --> 20:34.066
Damn, bro,
you've worked a lot of part-time jobs.

20:34.149 --> 20:35.567
- Are you poor?
- Mm-hm.

20:35.651 --> 20:37.110
My family lost everything.

20:39.529 --> 20:40.447
How?

20:42.908 --> 20:45.285
My dad was a researcher
for a large corporation.

20:45.369 --> 20:47.913
He sued them for wrongful termination
and ended up losing the suit.

20:48.914 --> 20:51.291
Legal fees from back then all became debt.

20:52.292 --> 20:54.795
You can't beat the big companies.
The rich always come out on top.

20:54.878 --> 20:55.921
That's true.

20:58.632 --> 21:01.593
- What were your other gigs?
- Well, I dabbled in this and that.

21:01.677 --> 21:03.595
For the most part,
I made deliveries with my mom.

21:04.763 --> 21:06.306
I guess you're a world-class part-timer.

21:09.142 --> 21:10.477
Oh!

21:10.560 --> 21:13.063
You are good at everything.
You've led a good life.

21:13.605 --> 21:15.148
I see you grill with your right hand.

21:16.275 --> 21:17.609
So when did you start boxing?

21:18.318 --> 21:20.237
Uh, about three years ago.

21:20.320 --> 21:22.322
- After school?
- After my military service.

21:22.406 --> 21:23.573
Ah…

21:24.074 --> 21:26.326
I first put on my gloves
for the first time in sixth grade.

21:26.410 --> 21:28.036
My dad was on the national team.

21:28.120 --> 21:30.163
Wow, that's so cool.

21:30.247 --> 21:31.581
And so what's your father's name?

21:31.665 --> 21:32.541
Hong Seong-geun.

21:33.166 --> 21:34.543
Barcelona bronze medalist.

21:34.626 --> 21:36.211
- Oh.
- Know him?

21:36.295 --> 21:37.421
No.

21:38.505 --> 21:40.090
Most boxers seem to know him.

21:40.173 --> 21:42.175
Oh. Sorry.

21:43.635 --> 21:45.470
I assume
your dad taught you how to box, right?

21:46.179 --> 21:47.264
We aren't that close.

21:48.140 --> 21:48.974
Why?

21:49.474 --> 21:51.476
My dad is never satisfied
with anything that I do.

21:52.311 --> 21:54.104
He won his bronze medal at my age,

21:54.938 --> 21:57.149
so he judges me
based on his accomplishments.

21:57.649 --> 21:58.817
Hm.

21:59.568 --> 22:01.069
So you're basically saying

22:01.570 --> 22:03.405
that your dad won a bronze medal
at the Olympics

22:03.488 --> 22:04.990
when he was only twenty-five years old?

22:06.116 --> 22:07.659
No, twenty-seven.

22:10.787 --> 22:12.289
Oh, how old are you?

22:12.873 --> 22:14.082
Twenty-seven.

22:14.166 --> 22:15.250
Uh,

22:15.876 --> 22:18.920
I'm sorry, man. I'm actually twenty-five.
I'm sorry. Please forgive my manners.

22:19.004 --> 22:20.797
Ah, you ass!

22:20.881 --> 22:21.715
Please forgive me.

22:21.798 --> 22:22.841
- Hey.
- Yes?

22:22.924 --> 22:24.634
Learn to respect your elders, got it?

22:24.718 --> 22:25.969
- Yes.
- Understand?

22:26.511 --> 22:27.346
Sure.

22:28.013 --> 22:28.930
Flip it now.

22:29.014 --> 22:31.308
Oh, not yet.
It still needs one more minute.

22:31.391 --> 22:33.560
- I said to flip it.
- I can't do that.

22:33.643 --> 22:37.189
Oh god, you are one stubborn punk, bro.
You've served in the army?

22:37.272 --> 22:40.233
Yes, I told you earlier I started boxing
after I finished my military service.

22:40.317 --> 22:41.610
Yeah, you did.

22:41.693 --> 22:43.779
What I mean is,
where were you stationed, huh?

22:43.862 --> 22:45.113
- Oh.
- You need to learn to keep up.

22:45.197 --> 22:47.282
Um, yes, I was in the Marine Corps.

22:48.492 --> 22:51.203
Hey! I'm a marine too!

22:51.703 --> 22:52.621
Oh.

22:52.704 --> 22:53.705
What class?

22:53.789 --> 22:56.083
Uh, I was in the 1,207th class.

22:58.335 --> 23:01.046
Sir! I was in the 1,216th class, sir!

23:01.129 --> 23:03.882
What are you doing? Sit. Please sit.

23:03.965 --> 23:05.592
I will sit when you return my salute, sir.

23:05.675 --> 23:06.968
Oh, uh…

23:10.680 --> 23:12.015
So you're Marine Kim Gun-woo.

23:12.099 --> 23:13.809
- Mm.
- So which division did you serve?

23:14.393 --> 23:15.268
The First Division.

23:15.352 --> 23:17.270
Me too! Which battalion were you in, sir?

23:18.480 --> 23:20.774
- Recon.
- Amazing.

23:21.441 --> 23:24.403
I also wanted to get into reconnaissance,
but I didn't make the cut.

23:24.486 --> 23:27.114
- Mm.
- The pride of the Marines, recon.

23:27.697 --> 23:29.366
Recon!

23:29.866 --> 23:30.742
Ah!

23:30.826 --> 23:33.495
You can still call me "bro," okay?
Let's just speak casually.

23:34.538 --> 23:35.664
I understand, sir.

23:35.747 --> 23:37.040
Yeah, but let's be casual.

23:37.124 --> 23:38.583
Casual it is, sir.

23:38.667 --> 23:39.626
Bro.

23:39.709 --> 23:40.544
Hm?

23:41.086 --> 23:41.920
Here.

23:45.006 --> 23:49.261
Yeah, I have a crazy amount of pride
as a marine.

23:49.344 --> 23:50.178
Why?

23:50.262 --> 23:52.722
I was kind of a thug back in Incheon,

23:52.806 --> 23:53.974
but I joined the Marine Corps,

23:54.057 --> 23:55.767
met some nice people,
and came to my senses.

23:55.851 --> 23:57.102
I just loved it all.

23:57.185 --> 24:00.897
Going through tough training together
and overcoming it all.

24:00.981 --> 24:02.315
This looks delicious.

24:02.899 --> 24:05.402
Waking up in the morning,
going on runs, sweating bullets,

24:05.485 --> 24:07.028
then showering together,

24:07.112 --> 24:09.072
washing each, all that, you know.

24:09.990 --> 24:12.492
- You're one of those crazy marines?
- Of course not.

24:12.576 --> 24:13.743
You have to try this.

24:16.329 --> 24:17.289
How is it? How is it?

24:19.749 --> 24:21.168
It's practically steak.

24:21.251 --> 24:23.128
Really?

24:23.712 --> 24:24.796
Let me show you something.

24:26.047 --> 24:27.257
- Watch this.
- Wow, yes.

24:27.340 --> 24:29.301
- Three pieces with ssamjang.
- Yes, yes, yes, yes.

24:29.384 --> 24:30.719
Want some kimchi with that too?

24:33.847 --> 24:35.015
Ah, ah.

24:35.098 --> 24:37.058
- Marine Kim Gun-woo, sir.
- Yeah?

24:40.395 --> 24:41.271
Mm. Mm.

24:41.354 --> 24:43.565
- Amazing. Amazing, right?
- Uh-huh. Mm-hm

24:43.648 --> 24:45.025
- Want to get some soju?
- No.

24:45.108 --> 24:46.985
- Why? Because of your diet?
- Mm-hm.

24:47.068 --> 24:48.487
You're such a perfectionist.

24:48.570 --> 24:50.322
You're too much.

24:50.405 --> 24:51.239
Excuse me!

24:51.740 --> 24:52.657
A beer!

24:52.741 --> 24:55.785
Please. Ah!

24:57.454 --> 24:59.122
Bro, how much were your shoes?

24:59.623 --> 25:01.041
- 1.2 mill.
- Seriously?

25:01.541 --> 25:04.211
Why so expensive?
That's a month's rent for our store.

25:04.294 --> 25:05.837
Damn, you are really gullible.

25:05.921 --> 25:07.339
Obviously they're knockoffs.

25:08.965 --> 25:10.050
Well, they look real.

25:10.592 --> 25:12.344
Knockoffs have shiny toe caps, see?

25:12.427 --> 25:13.845
And the real ones are suede.

25:13.929 --> 25:15.972
The threads around the holes
are pretty shitty too.

25:16.973 --> 25:18.183
Tell me if you wanna buy some.

25:18.266 --> 25:19.809
I can get you better than the real thing.

25:19.893 --> 25:21.895
- Really?
- Are you shitting me? No, bro.

25:21.978 --> 25:25.148
There's nothing in the world
that tops the real deal, all right?

25:26.191 --> 25:28.902
You should hang out with me more,
so we can work on your street smarts.

25:28.985 --> 25:30.820
You spend too much time
on your part-time jobs.

25:33.281 --> 25:36.368
Do you know about this?
I heard it's very common these days.

25:36.451 --> 25:38.954
"COVID-19 special loans."

25:39.037 --> 25:40.372
COVID-19 SUPPORT
SUPER LOW-INTEREST SPECIAL LOAN

25:40.455 --> 25:41.581
Back in the day,

25:41.665 --> 25:45.710
I was so strapped for cash,
that I worked in money lending.

25:45.794 --> 25:47.629
Desperate people are easier to rip off.

25:47.712 --> 25:50.006
The pandemic has made
many people desperate.

25:52.175 --> 25:55.011
So I guess now
all the loan sharks have come out to play.

25:55.095 --> 25:55.929
Really?

25:56.012 --> 25:58.848
Since everyone is rushing
to cover their rent,

25:58.932 --> 26:01.393
all the sharks need to do
is shake their hand and suck them dry.

26:03.311 --> 26:06.606
My mom is also having a hard time
because of the rent payments for her café.

26:07.232 --> 26:09.901
The business makes less than a fourth
of what we used to,

26:09.985 --> 26:12.028
but the landlord still takes
the same amount of rent.

26:13.655 --> 26:15.907
If we close down now,
it would cost us more to move out,

26:15.991 --> 26:17.867
so we're just trying to stay afloat.

26:17.951 --> 26:20.579
Apparently, you have to return the store
to its original state.

26:21.413 --> 26:22.664
Damn.

26:26.835 --> 26:27.669
Here.

26:29.838 --> 26:32.299
I'll treat you
to something real fancy next time.

26:33.341 --> 26:35.468
- Are we gonna have rib eye?
- Ah, just come with me.

26:35.552 --> 26:37.012
I know a good barbecue place.

26:37.095 --> 26:38.346
You aren't messing with me?

26:38.430 --> 26:42.392
Hey, do you think I would tell
such a low-level lie to a senior marine?

26:42.475 --> 26:45.437
- I think you would.
- So you don't believe me?

26:45.520 --> 26:47.939
I just mean
because you've been lying to me all day.

26:48.023 --> 26:50.817
Man, those were just jokes.

26:50.900 --> 26:52.611
All right, I promise no more lies.

26:53.903 --> 26:55.113
Deal.

26:55.905 --> 26:57.157
I know.

26:57.782 --> 26:59.117
I am so sorry.

26:59.200 --> 27:00.410
I tried my best.

27:00.994 --> 27:02.495
I just couldn't…

27:03.163 --> 27:04.789
…get it together in time.

27:05.540 --> 27:09.836
Yes, if I just get through this month,
I will come up with it somehow.

27:11.004 --> 27:12.255
Again, I am sorry.

27:13.840 --> 27:15.091
Oh, uh, sorry.

27:15.175 --> 27:17.052
- Let me call you back in the morning.
- Mom!

27:18.178 --> 27:20.305
My boy!

27:20.388 --> 27:21.973
Oh my boy!

27:23.933 --> 27:25.894
Look at you. You were incredible today.

27:25.977 --> 27:28.188
- You watched it?
- Oh, of course I watched it.

27:28.271 --> 27:30.982
The commentators kept talking about you
the whole time.

27:31.066 --> 27:33.818
- Are you serious?
- Yes, they kept saying you're perfect.

27:33.902 --> 27:36.404
So I guess I should watch it too then.

27:36.488 --> 27:37.530
- Mom, hold on.
- Look at you.

27:37.614 --> 27:39.240
I'm so proud of you.

27:40.241 --> 27:41.368
Here.

27:42.243 --> 27:43.203
What's that?

27:43.912 --> 27:46.039
The prize, so we can pay the rent.

27:48.375 --> 27:49.459
Oh.

27:50.043 --> 27:51.878
Oh, no, no. I can't take this.

27:53.546 --> 27:55.465
No, Mom, I won this to give it to you.

27:58.927 --> 28:01.930
Let's pay… Uncle back first
for what we owe.

28:04.724 --> 28:06.643
How… how do you know about your uncle?

28:06.726 --> 28:10.021
He's also going through a lot, Mom.
Let's pay him back.

28:14.651 --> 28:15.610
All right.

28:16.611 --> 28:19.531
But listen, I will pay you back for this
with interest.

28:19.614 --> 28:23.076
- Okay.
- Oh, thank you.

28:26.329 --> 28:29.249
- Let's go, Mom.
- Ah, it's so cold. Let's go.

28:30.375 --> 28:31.334
Did you eat?

28:31.418 --> 28:32.377
Yeah, of course.

28:32.460 --> 28:33.837
Oh, with who?

28:34.421 --> 28:35.672
The guy I fought in the finals.

28:37.549 --> 28:40.844
Oh, the boy with the curly hair?

28:40.927 --> 28:41.886
Yeah, that one.

28:42.971 --> 28:45.014
Mom, did you eat?

28:45.098 --> 28:46.558
Oh, sure, sure. I ate.

29:05.243 --> 29:06.077
Sir.

29:06.661 --> 29:07.579
How are things?

29:08.455 --> 29:09.748
Sir, as you predicted,

29:09.831 --> 29:12.876
all tenants owed money to banks
or second-tier financial companies.

29:13.626 --> 29:16.671
So my plan is to bring all of them to us
by next week.

29:16.755 --> 29:19.591
Okay, can you make it happen by this week?

29:20.216 --> 29:23.011
Assemblyman Seo keeps badgering me
to kick them out quickly.

29:23.762 --> 29:25.555
I'll see what I can do, sir.

29:25.638 --> 29:27.766
Yes, let's hurry things along.

29:28.308 --> 29:30.310
The sales team's operations are key,
aren't they?

29:31.102 --> 29:31.936
Yes, they are.

29:36.524 --> 29:37.609
Beom, listen.

29:39.694 --> 29:40.653
Let's get ready.

30:00.256 --> 30:03.343
I am team manager Yoo In-yeong
from Smile Capital.

30:03.426 --> 30:05.386
We are a financial company

30:05.470 --> 30:07.847
that was recently government-certified
for excellence,

30:07.931 --> 30:11.267
and I was wondering
if you had some time for a quick chat.

30:11.351 --> 30:12.185
Okay.

30:12.769 --> 30:15.939
Your business doesn't get many visitors
these days, huh?

30:17.440 --> 30:18.358
No.

30:18.441 --> 30:21.194
I believe you owe the bank 40 million won.
Is that accurate, sir?

30:21.820 --> 30:22.654
Yeah.

30:22.737 --> 30:26.115
Once you sign here,
we will pay off that debt today.

30:27.200 --> 30:31.454
And we have an interest rate of 5%
which is way lower than the bank's 7%.

30:31.538 --> 30:34.457
Doesn't that end up leaving you
without any actual profit?

30:34.541 --> 30:35.458
That's true.

30:35.542 --> 30:39.003
But, uh, the government has started
a special support project

30:39.087 --> 30:40.922
to help the small business owners

30:41.005 --> 30:43.132
who are struggling
because of the pandemic.

30:43.216 --> 30:44.217
We won a support package,

30:44.300 --> 30:47.178
which allows us to lower interest rates
even more than the other companies.

30:47.262 --> 30:50.139
A 2% difference in interest
is not a small amount

30:50.765 --> 30:53.810
In times like these,
just staying afloat is winning.

30:54.727 --> 30:57.230
We know this pandemic will pass soon.

30:57.313 --> 30:58.565
DEBT REPAYMENT
AND NEW CONTRACT AGREEMENT

30:58.648 --> 31:01.234
But we want to extend
whatever help we can,

31:01.317 --> 31:02.819
so that you can keep your business.

31:05.405 --> 31:07.073
It's true this is good for us too.

31:07.156 --> 31:09.367
but it's really good for you, sir,

31:12.412 --> 31:14.873
- Yes, thank you.
- Thank you so much.

31:14.956 --> 31:16.374
SMILE CAPITAL
SIGNEE YOON SO-YEON

31:32.599 --> 31:33.558
Huh?

31:33.641 --> 31:35.059
TEMPORARILY CLOSED
DUE TO A CONFIRMED COVID-19 PATIENT

31:35.143 --> 31:38.938
We had dinner last night
with some of the other members at the gym.

31:39.022 --> 31:41.024
Apparently, one of them tested positive.

31:42.066 --> 31:44.444
Oh, do you think I should get tested too?

31:44.527 --> 31:45.528
No, you're fine.

31:45.612 --> 31:48.406
Anyway, your match was just yesterday.

31:48.489 --> 31:50.116
Why did I hear
that you're back at the gym?

31:50.199 --> 31:52.577
- To work out. Why else?
- Gun-woo.

31:53.161 --> 31:54.370
Please take a week off and rest.

31:54.996 --> 31:56.247
Rest doing what?

31:56.331 --> 31:58.958
Nothing. If you're doing something,
you're not resting.

31:59.042 --> 32:00.793
Just don't do anything and try to relax.

32:01.544 --> 32:02.378
Okay.

32:12.889 --> 32:15.224
GU-NOO

32:22.982 --> 32:24.567
Uh, what are you up to?

32:26.361 --> 32:27.570
Sleep.

32:27.654 --> 32:30.073
- Huh?
- Sleeping.

32:31.199 --> 32:33.618
- Uh, I can't hear you.
- Sleep, sleeping.

32:33.701 --> 32:35.995
I am sleeping.

32:36.663 --> 32:40.333
- Well, do you want to work out?
- No.

32:40.875 --> 32:42.168
Ah, but I'm bored.

32:42.251 --> 32:45.421
God, so clingy so early in the morning.

32:46.005 --> 32:47.340
Let's hang out. Hm?

32:50.093 --> 32:52.762
I'll send my address. Come.

32:52.845 --> 32:54.639
Okay, sounds good.

33:11.030 --> 33:12.073
Oh shit!

33:12.824 --> 33:14.659
Fuck! Goddammit. Stop!

33:15.243 --> 33:16.494
You son of a bitch!

34:01.622 --> 34:04.083
Are you all right?

34:04.167 --> 34:05.293
Uh, okay, wait here.

34:32.737 --> 34:33.571
Who?

34:33.654 --> 34:34.530
Huh?

34:35.156 --> 34:36.491
Why'd you follow me?

34:37.158 --> 34:38.284
Tell me who sent you.

34:39.952 --> 34:42.580
To help.

34:42.663 --> 34:44.999
What? Help who?

34:46.250 --> 34:48.878
I thought that man was being chased,

34:48.961 --> 34:50.671
and, uh, I didn't know what was going on.

34:50.755 --> 34:52.882
- God fucking dammit.
- Huh?

34:52.965 --> 34:54.759
That asshole is a fake.

34:54.842 --> 34:57.261
- Huh?
- Just butt out of things you don't know.

34:57.345 --> 34:59.806
Motherfucker.

35:04.936 --> 35:05.770
Huh?

35:35.216 --> 35:36.134
What brings you here?

35:36.217 --> 35:38.052
Everything went well.

35:38.136 --> 35:40.179
I mean with Mi-yeon's surgery yesterday.

35:40.263 --> 35:42.431
Oh, really? And how is she doing now?

35:43.015 --> 35:44.058
She's good, sir.

35:44.142 --> 35:46.060
She's recovering very well.

35:48.312 --> 35:49.981
It's all thanks to you.

35:50.773 --> 35:52.733
If you hadn't helped us back then, sir,

35:53.234 --> 35:55.778
my daughter might have died.

35:59.365 --> 36:00.199
Here.

36:02.076 --> 36:05.163
My husband had the good fortune
of moving over to a larger company,

36:05.246 --> 36:07.415
so he just received his severance.

36:08.833 --> 36:11.085
I came here
as soon as the money hit our accounts

36:11.169 --> 36:14.172
because I wanted to pay you back
before I paid anyone else.

36:17.550 --> 36:19.260
You can take your time to pay me back.

36:20.803 --> 36:22.305
First, pay back your urgent debts.

36:22.889 --> 36:23.890
Oh, no, sir.

36:23.973 --> 36:26.517
Please. Please accept this.

36:27.310 --> 36:29.478
I finally have some peace of mind.

36:32.440 --> 36:33.983
Thank you so much, sir.

36:35.860 --> 36:38.404
Thank you so much. Thank you so much.

36:41.115 --> 36:43.326
Thank you.

36:58.841 --> 37:00.968
MI-YEON'S MOTHER APRIL 14TH, 2018
20 MILLION WON

37:06.766 --> 37:12.813
KOREAN ANTIQUE MALL

37:32.750 --> 37:34.168
I found Yang Jae-myeong.

37:34.252 --> 37:36.671
He tried telling me he had no money,

37:36.754 --> 37:38.047
so I took this from him.

37:42.093 --> 37:43.970
This watch goes for over 20 million won.

37:44.053 --> 37:45.096
So what?

37:46.013 --> 37:48.099
Yang Jae-myeong borrowed ten million won.

37:49.100 --> 37:50.559
Yeah, plus interest.

37:56.190 --> 37:57.233
Oh, did you get hurt?

37:57.316 --> 37:59.777
I got in a scuffle
with Yang Jae-myeong.

38:00.778 --> 38:03.281
By the way,
while we're already on the subject,

38:03.364 --> 38:04.532
you and I need to talk.

38:04.615 --> 38:05.825
Have some rice cakes first.

38:06.742 --> 38:09.203
We need to talk.
Don't try to change the subject.

38:11.580 --> 38:13.040
How long are you going to keep at it?

38:14.458 --> 38:15.293
What?

38:17.336 --> 38:19.255
Lending people money with no interest.

38:19.338 --> 38:21.007
I mean, it's not profitable.

38:21.507 --> 38:22.591
What do you mean by that?

38:22.675 --> 38:25.886
I always pay you
your 30% in commission fees.

38:25.970 --> 38:28.139
Not for me. For you, Grandpa.

38:32.059 --> 38:33.686
You know Mi-yeon's mother?

38:34.812 --> 38:35.813
Yeah, and?

38:35.896 --> 38:39.400
She dropped by earlier
and paid back the entire sum in cash.

38:41.319 --> 38:42.403
And that's the interest?

38:44.780 --> 38:45.698
Hyeon-ju.

38:46.282 --> 38:48.951
A sick child got a timely operation
that saved her.

38:49.035 --> 38:50.578
Because I lent them money,

38:50.661 --> 38:53.706
her parents didn't have to use their home
as collateral for a loan.

38:53.789 --> 38:57.209
And now, when their child's better,
she has a home to go to.

38:58.627 --> 39:00.338
You and I saved a family.

39:01.380 --> 39:04.133
This is the most precious form of interest
in the world.

39:07.762 --> 39:09.889
Well, anyway, I heard something

39:09.972 --> 39:12.058
while digging around
for Yang Jae-myeong's whereabouts.

39:12.933 --> 39:15.436
He and his crew are dressing up
as homeless people

39:15.519 --> 39:18.064
and robbing the actual homeless
of their IDs

39:18.147 --> 39:19.398
to take out loans in their names.

39:19.482 --> 39:21.108
And who are these people?

39:21.192 --> 39:23.361
They're not exactly the cream of the crop.

39:23.444 --> 39:24.445
They met in prison.

39:24.528 --> 39:26.489
You knew this,
and you went all by yourself?

39:27.365 --> 39:29.033
Should I have you tag along next time?

39:29.116 --> 39:31.827
Anyway, let me do some digging.

39:32.495 --> 39:34.121
I think I will find something interesting.

39:34.205 --> 39:36.040
As long as you're not in danger, okay?

39:36.624 --> 39:37.500
Sure.

39:47.468 --> 39:50.513
PRESIDENT MOON GWANG-MU

39:50.596 --> 39:52.723
MARINE
IF IT DOESN'T WORK, MAKE IT WORK!

39:52.807 --> 39:53.641
Hello?

39:53.724 --> 39:56.519
Hi. Oh, is this a bad time?

39:56.602 --> 39:57.812
No, sir. No, please go ahead.

39:57.895 --> 40:00.898
Yes, I wanted to ask you a favor
to find someone.

40:00.981 --> 40:02.066
One second, please.

40:03.859 --> 40:04.860
All right, I'm listening.

40:05.945 --> 40:06.946
"A good person."

40:08.239 --> 40:09.698
"A skilled bodyguard

40:10.783 --> 40:13.327
who is familiar with the loan business."

40:16.580 --> 40:17.790
All right, sir.

40:18.290 --> 40:20.876
I will find the best candidates.
I promise I will find the best.

40:21.460 --> 40:22.795
I'll leave it in your hands.

40:22.878 --> 40:24.839
Yes, sir. Anytime.

40:26.757 --> 40:29.093
Mayweather is the top dog. No doubt.

40:29.176 --> 40:31.345
But Mayweather feels
more like a businessman

40:31.429 --> 40:32.513
than an actual boxer.

40:32.596 --> 40:33.431
That's right.

40:33.514 --> 40:36.475
My guy's in it for the money,
but he is ridiculously good at it.

40:37.184 --> 40:39.019
Probably made a few hundred billion.

40:39.562 --> 40:40.813
Does money matter to you?

40:41.939 --> 40:43.399
What could matter more than money?

40:44.108 --> 40:45.234
The heart of a boxer.

40:48.362 --> 40:49.238
What?

40:51.907 --> 40:54.118
What?

40:56.036 --> 40:58.914
- Dude.
- No, No. Sorry.

41:00.124 --> 41:02.042
It's just you got so serious
all of a sudden.

41:02.126 --> 41:04.587
You looked so serious
that it really caught me off guard.

41:05.087 --> 41:06.922
Elaborate on this boxer's heart.

41:07.506 --> 41:08.382
Hm.

41:09.633 --> 41:11.969
I think Manny Pacquiao
is the best example because--

41:12.052 --> 41:15.347
Pow! Pow, pow, Pacquiao! Pow, pow.

41:15.431 --> 41:18.684
Come on, dude. Let me have my moment.
I never cut you off, man.

41:19.435 --> 41:22.646
I'm sorry, marine.
I will never cut you off.

41:22.730 --> 41:26.984
Well, I really admire Pacquiao's heart,
you know? He never gives up.

41:27.067 --> 41:30.779
Okay, I can give him that,
but Mayweather made a lot more money.

41:30.863 --> 41:34.700
But I bet a lot more kids started dreaming
of becoming a boxer because of Pacquiao.

41:34.783 --> 41:36.202
That's true for me at least.

41:37.661 --> 41:40.581
That's the kind of person I want to be.

41:40.664 --> 41:44.210
A person who shows
that with strong will and undying passion,

41:44.293 --> 41:46.253
anyone will be able to achieve
all of their dreams.

41:46.337 --> 41:47.838
It's windy today.

41:47.922 --> 41:50.007
That is a true boxer's heart

41:50.090 --> 41:53.636
and the kind of hope we should inspire
in the people watching us.

41:54.553 --> 41:56.180
- A boxer's heart--
- Hey, this is ready.

41:56.263 --> 41:57.223
Let's eat.

41:59.391 --> 42:00.226
Here.

42:05.731 --> 42:07.441
- Is it good?
- So good.

42:08.776 --> 42:10.861
Hey, what do you do for a living?

42:10.945 --> 42:14.949
I used to teach gym classes
at a kindergarten my friend runs.

42:15.032 --> 42:16.534
A gym teacher of sorts.

42:17.076 --> 42:18.577
Ah, that doesn't suit you, right?

42:18.661 --> 42:19.870
What do you mean?

42:20.704 --> 42:21.872
Kids fucking love me.

42:22.456 --> 42:24.416
Well, anyway,
I used to do that in the morning,

42:24.500 --> 42:26.043
then worked out in the afternoons.

42:26.126 --> 42:27.962
Since the kindergarten shut down,
I'm in a bind.

42:30.339 --> 42:32.299
Hey, wanna go on deliveries with me?

42:32.383 --> 42:34.176
You can make some serious money
on parcel runs.

42:35.177 --> 42:36.679
- Is the pay good?
- Yeah.

42:36.762 --> 42:38.347
If we put our minds to it,

42:38.430 --> 42:40.808
we could probably make 200,000 each.

42:40.891 --> 42:41.767
For real?

42:41.850 --> 42:43.852
Yeah, delivery work is also good cardio.

42:43.936 --> 42:45.771
And you get to work on
your non-boxing muscles,

42:45.854 --> 42:47.189
so it's good for your balance too.

42:47.273 --> 42:50.693
- Ah, killing two birds with one stone.
- Three birds.

42:50.776 --> 42:51.610
Huh?

42:51.694 --> 42:54.613
You make money, get your cardio in,
and work on your balance.

42:54.697 --> 42:57.199
Yeah, cardio and balance are the same.

42:57.283 --> 42:59.034
Uh, no, they're not.

43:01.036 --> 43:04.456
Wait, but aren't you supposed to compete
in the Super Series

43:04.540 --> 43:06.417
since you won
the Rookie of the Year tournament?

43:06.917 --> 43:09.837
Mm-hm, but it's been postponed
due to COVID.

43:12.339 --> 43:14.633
How much longer?

43:15.342 --> 43:16.594
There's nothing I can do.

43:19.430 --> 43:23.183
Except I'll make sure I'm ready to fight
whenever the time actually comes.

43:26.228 --> 43:29.732
You know… you have a boxer's heart.

43:35.904 --> 43:38.449
Hm?

43:38.532 --> 43:40.409
- Come on, Pacquiao.
- Right now?

43:47.249 --> 43:48.125
Whoa…

43:49.293 --> 43:50.753
Man, how could you hit me for real?

43:50.836 --> 43:52.046
Whoa, my bad. Sorry.

43:52.129 --> 43:53.589
Hey, come here, come here. Come here.

43:53.672 --> 43:54.757
Let go. Let go.

43:54.840 --> 43:57.926
- Come here. Let go. Come here. Come here.
- Whoa! Whoa!

43:58.010 --> 44:00.137
Come here. Hey, Kim Gun-woo!

44:01.013 --> 44:04.266
Everyone, cheers!

44:07.728 --> 44:10.981
Now for today's main event.
The greatest show on Earth!

44:11.065 --> 44:13.859
Cracking a watermelon with In-beom!

44:13.942 --> 44:17.154
Everyone, come on! Make your bets now!

44:17.237 --> 44:18.530
A million that he fails!

44:19.448 --> 44:23.285
Hey! Three million on his success.

44:24.119 --> 44:27.665
And if I'm the winner of this pot,
everything is on me!

44:27.748 --> 44:29.291
Beom,
I know you can crack it,

44:29.375 --> 44:31.710
but I'm gonna bet four million
that you can't

44:33.879 --> 44:36.465
- Kang In-beom!
- Let's go!

44:36.548 --> 44:39.176
- Kang In-beom!
- Kang In-beom!

44:39.259 --> 44:41.220
Kang In-beom!

44:43.138 --> 44:44.014
He cracked it!

44:46.058 --> 44:47.810
Tteokbokki for all! Yeah!

44:47.893 --> 44:49.687
Let's have some tteokbokki!

44:49.770 --> 44:50.854
Awesome job!

44:50.938 --> 44:51.855
Woo!

44:51.939 --> 44:53.357
I did well, didn't I?

44:53.440 --> 44:54.692
DEAREST MAYOR

44:56.944 --> 44:58.612
Shh. Quiet. Quiet!

45:05.160 --> 45:06.161
Yes, Mr. Mayor.

45:08.539 --> 45:09.873
Yes.

45:12.668 --> 45:13.669
Yes.

45:17.715 --> 45:18.716
Yes.

45:20.217 --> 45:21.427
I understand, sir.

45:21.510 --> 45:22.803
I will let him know.

45:23.929 --> 45:25.264
Have a good evening, sir.

45:29.143 --> 45:31.812
The mayor… has just decided that

45:33.564 --> 45:34.732
he will back the casino bid.

45:35.566 --> 45:37.443
- Yes.
- Yes!

45:43.198 --> 45:49.037
I have prepared… a small gift for you,
Mr. Park, in honor of your birthday.

45:54.585 --> 45:55.419
Open it.

46:02.009 --> 46:03.635
Almost four kilos.

46:04.720 --> 46:09.725
Mr. Park, these gold turtles are so clean
that no one will know if you have them.

46:10.809 --> 46:12.311
I give you this with the hope

46:12.394 --> 46:15.314
that our relationship will continue
for a long time.

46:15.397 --> 46:18.734
So I would appreciate if you take them.

46:27.534 --> 46:29.912
You don't want to be in City Hall forever.

46:31.580 --> 46:33.457
I know you have big dreams, Mr. Park.

46:33.540 --> 46:36.543
If you plan on going
to the National Assembly,

46:36.627 --> 46:38.212
you will definitely need money.

46:39.171 --> 46:40.923
Let us forge a lasting partnership.

46:41.423 --> 46:43.801
I will support you every way I can.

46:45.469 --> 46:48.931
My money never has known failure.
You can rest assured.

47:03.028 --> 47:05.906
- Hey. Hey!
- Jeez.

47:06.406 --> 47:08.408
Hey, where are we going?

47:08.492 --> 47:10.994
Please get in carefully.
We'll take you home.

47:11.078 --> 47:12.538
Let's go.

47:18.502 --> 47:20.379
And Assemblyman Seo's building?

47:21.129 --> 47:22.840
Just wait until Friday, sir.

47:23.549 --> 47:26.176
All the stores will have
over 20 million in interest.

47:26.677 --> 47:28.720
I think the small stores
need a little grilling.

47:29.221 --> 47:31.181
People tend to give up faster

47:31.265 --> 47:34.309
if they see their first-floor storefront
in complete shambles

47:34.393 --> 47:36.478
every time they come into work, you know?

47:38.313 --> 47:39.565
I'll do as you wish, sir.

47:40.858 --> 47:43.527
Since Mr. Jung is not feeling well
and can't join you,

47:43.610 --> 47:46.488
call them and tell them to send over
15 intimidating men.

47:46.572 --> 47:48.031
Beom can wrap things up.

47:48.115 --> 47:49.575
Should they be armed?

47:50.158 --> 47:51.201
There's no need.

47:51.285 --> 47:54.204
Tell them to suit up
and make sure that everyone is masked.

47:54.288 --> 47:56.456
Sir, I think five men should be enough.

47:56.540 --> 47:59.501
I'm sure that the boss has his reasons.

48:01.503 --> 48:02.754
You're right.

48:03.380 --> 48:04.631
I've made a huge mistake.

48:07.593 --> 48:09.595
You shitheads, there you go again.

48:09.678 --> 48:11.471
Come on. Focus.

48:12.806 --> 48:13.932
Where should we begin?

48:51.261 --> 48:52.095
Huh?

48:52.888 --> 48:54.890
Oh, hello. Good evening.

48:55.933 --> 48:57.225
Why didn't you keep your promise?

48:58.852 --> 48:59.686
What?

48:59.770 --> 49:01.521
You agreed to an extension fee

49:02.814 --> 49:04.650
in exchange for a lowered interest rate.

49:05.233 --> 49:06.401
Uh, what?

49:07.861 --> 49:12.699
But you needed to pay that extension fee,
which is 10% of the principal,

49:13.283 --> 49:14.910
within 24 hours of signing.

49:14.993 --> 49:16.828
It says so on the contract.

49:16.912 --> 49:18.956
But because you failed to do so,

49:19.831 --> 49:22.459
your extension
has accrued 40 million in interest.

49:22.542 --> 49:24.252
Not to mention
your credit score has dropped,

49:24.336 --> 49:26.713
so your interest rate has gone up to 20%.

49:27.339 --> 49:32.177
We really… started
with the purest of intentions.

49:33.387 --> 49:35.389
You ruined everything, damn it!

49:37.683 --> 49:39.142
What are you going to do now?

49:40.143 --> 49:41.561
Do you have that kind of money?

49:45.273 --> 49:46.692
I will call the police.

49:47.609 --> 49:48.443
Police?

49:50.195 --> 49:51.196
Yeah.

50:02.833 --> 50:04.001
Oh my God.

50:11.174 --> 50:12.300
Hey, Mom.

50:12.384 --> 50:13.927
Hey, son, where are you?

50:14.011 --> 50:17.431
- I'm almost there.
- Okay, I'm at the store.

50:17.514 --> 50:19.599
And a bunch of strange people came over…

50:19.683 --> 50:21.476
Strange people? Who?

50:21.560 --> 50:22.644
They're still here.

50:23.603 --> 50:26.231
Mom? What's going on?

50:59.222 --> 51:01.224
Where the hell
do you think you're going?

51:01.308 --> 51:04.061
Who the hell are you? Get lost!

51:05.145 --> 51:07.314
Hey! I told you to scram, asshole!

51:09.733 --> 51:11.401
This jackass! Hey, you!

51:13.195 --> 51:15.363
- What's going on? Get him.
- You shithead!

51:15.447 --> 51:17.115
Who the hell is this guy?

51:30.253 --> 51:31.129
Fuck!

51:32.464 --> 51:33.882
- Come here.
- Little shit!

52:25.183 --> 52:27.561
- Mom, are you all right?
- Yes.

52:27.644 --> 52:28.687
You aren't hurt, are you?

52:28.770 --> 52:31.523
I'm okay. I'm okay.

52:41.491 --> 52:42.409
Who are you?

52:43.869 --> 52:46.496
Who are you to do this to our store?

52:47.831 --> 52:49.708
I asked you, "Who are you?"

53:09.144 --> 53:10.478
Calm down, kid.

53:11.438 --> 53:14.733
Your mother has borrowed some money
from our company.

53:15.317 --> 53:17.611
Mm-hm

53:19.279 --> 53:20.447
So what do you want?

53:21.740 --> 53:22.949
Pay us back.

53:23.617 --> 53:25.368
Pay us for the damages first.

53:47.140 --> 53:48.225
Go ahead.

53:59.527 --> 54:01.905
Mom, it's okay.
Just go over there for a second.

54:01.988 --> 54:03.949
Gun-woo!

55:20.233 --> 55:21.651
Gun-woo!

55:50.055 --> 55:51.890
Gun-woo!

56:10.283 --> 56:11.117
That's enough.

56:35.058 --> 56:39.020
Hey, I appreciate people with grit.

56:40.897 --> 56:44.484
Because guys with grit…
They can get anything done.

56:47.737 --> 56:49.322
Do you want to work for me?

56:49.406 --> 56:50.907
I will make sure that…
